    {
      "id": 91357,
      "name": "Ronway",
      "username": "Ronway",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-02-14T04:34:44.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Nojh\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/858c86/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Nojh:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Can someone explain the first sentence of Setback's \"High Risk Behavior\" card using one sentence per +1 being assigned to a target (or in any way that makes it easier to parse)?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Basically, when Setback deals damage to a villain target, he increases it by 1 for every 3 tokens he has in his pool. So 9 tokens will give a +3. It also increases damage dealt by villain targets to Setback by 1 for every 3 tokens in his pool.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:16:57.881Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
