      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"Nojh\"]\n\nCan someone explain the first sentence of Setback&#39;s &quot;High Risk Behavior&quot; card using one sentence per +1 being assigned to a target (or in any way that makes it easier to parse)?\n\n[/quote]\n\nBasically, when Setback deals damage to a villain target, he increases it by 1 for every 3 tokens he has in his pool. So 9 tokens will give a +3. It also increases damage dealt by villain targets to Setback by 1 for every 3 tokens in his pool.\n",
