      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"cmschex\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/e9bcb4/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> cmschex:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wrong Time and Place also changed from the proof version, I noticed when playing last night. &nbsp;It's now the first time a hero target would take damage each turn, you can choose to redirect to Setback, who can then choose whether or not to redirect. &nbsp;It was a monster card playing against the V5 (and keeping the unlucky pool under control with Looking Up out)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I don't think you actually get to redirect it to Setback, if that card is in play you either redirect it to Setback or remove tokens to redirect it to another target. If you do not remove tokens, then Setback will be taking damage.</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
