      "created_at": "2014-08-04T12:46:46.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ringer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/7feea3/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ringer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hi all,&nbsp;I apologize for a slight thread necro, but I have a question that goes along with this card. &nbsp;How is the damage boost from high risk behaviour affected by token counts that aren't multiples of three. &nbsp;For example, if i have 4 unlucky tokens, am I at +1 or +2. &nbsp;In a broader sense, is there a stated rule for rounding numbers in Sentinels? &nbsp;I am not sure if there are other cards that would encounter this issue.Thanks! &nbsp;First Post!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You gain +1 for every three tokens. At 4 tokens your +damage is still just +1 until you get at least 6, then that second set of three tokens gives another +1, ect.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Welcome to the forums!</p>",
